[# Section 11 — Glossary. Back-matter; appears after §10 migration.
   Authored 2026-05-22.
   Every term in this glossary is used elsewhere in the guide; each
   entry cross-links to the section where the term is first
   introduced. Entries are alphabetical (case-insensitive). File
   extension .cxd — data-only source. #]

[section id=glossary n=11 title='Glossary'

  [intro
    """This is the working glossary for the CX data and code guide.
       Every domain-specific term used in §0–§10 is defined here, with
       a cross-link to the section where it is first introduced. If
       you encounter a term in this guide that is not defined here,
       file an issue — coverage is a release gate."""]

  [child id=g-anchor-sigil title='anchor sigil (&)'
    [body
      """The `&name` form on an element declares a named anchor. The
         anchor can be referenced later via the merge sigil `*name` to
         splice the anchored content. Declaring two anchors with the
         same name in one document raises `CXER0101`. See [[anchor]]."""]]

  [child id=g-array title='array'
    [body
      """A homogeneously-typed indexed container. Distinct from a
         sequence: arrays are atomic containers (one value), sequences
         are flat (no nesting). See [[arr]] and [[container-atom]]."""]]

  [child id=g-array-literal title='array literal'
    [body
      """Written `[a, b, c]` with commas inside square brackets — note
         that a CX element shares the bracket but has no leading comma
         after the element name. See [[arr]]."""]]

  [child id=g-ast-bin title='ast-bin'
    [body
      """The CX AST wire format — a compact binary serialisation of a
         parsed CX document including comments, whitespace, attribute
         order, and any author-annotated provenance. Used by tooling
         (LSP, diff, hash service). Distinct from data-bin, which is
         value-only. See [[ast-bin]]."""]]

  [child id=g-attribute title='attribute'
    [body
      """A `name=value` pair in an element header. The key is an
         identifier; the value is a bare scalar, quoted string,
         numeric literal, boolean, date, or `null`. Multiple
         attributes are space-separated. See [[attributes]]."""]]

  [child id=g-bcp47 title='BCP 47 tag'
    [body
      """A language identifier per IETF BCP 47 (e.g. `en-US`,
         `zh-Hant-TW`). Used as the value of the reserved
         `cx:lang` attribute. See [[locale]]."""]]

  [child id=g-binding title='binding (Layer 1, Layer 2)'
    [body
      """A host-language wrapper around the compiled `libcx`. Layer 1
         is the 16 canonical methods every binding must implement
         identically; Layer 2 is host-idiomatic syntactic sugar that
         varies per language. Currently ships V, Python, Go, and Rust.
         See [[bindings]]."""]]

  [child id=g-body title='body'
    [body
      """Everything between the attribute list and the closing `]` of
         an element. Can be empty, a single scalar, mixed content, or
         a sequence of nested elements. See [[bodies]]."""]]

  [child id=g-bool title='boolean'
    [body
      """The `true` / `false` scalar kind. Bare `true` and `false`
         are reserved tokens; booleans are ordinary `name=value`
         attributes — there is no shorthand sigil form. See
         [[booleans]] and [[bool]]."""]]

  [child id=g-bytes title='bytes'
    [body
      """A scalar kind holding raw binary data. Written as a
         length-prefixed base64 literal: `:bytes 'SGVsbG8='`. See
         [[bytes]] and [[bytes-wire]]."""]]

  [child id=g-canonical-bytes title='canonical bytes'
    [body
      """The unique byte sequence that represents a CX document after
         the canonicalization rules in
         [`spec/canonical.md`](../../spec/canonical.md) are applied.
         The SHA-256 of the canonical bytes is the document's
         identity. See [[canonical]]."""]]

  [child id=g-capability-bit title='capability bit'
    [body
      """A bit in the value returned by `cx_features()` that signals
         whether the loaded `libcx` supports a particular optional
         feature (Parquet bridge, diagram render, etc.). Bindings
         check before calling new entry points. See
         [[ast-bin-capabilities]]."""]]

  [child id=g-cdata title='CDATA'
    [body
      """An XML-only literal section that preserves arbitrary text
         verbatim. CX carries CDATA through the XML projection but
         re-encodes the content as a triple-quoted string in the
         canonical form. See [[cdata]]."""]]

  [child id=g-code-language title='code language'
    [body
      """The directive-based subset of CX. A code element is one whose
         name starts with `?` (e.g. `[?for]`). The evaluator
         dispatches on the directive name. Every other shape is data.
         See [[code]]."""]]

  [child id=g-comment title='comment'
    [body
      """`[# … #]` — nests, spans lines, allowed anywhere whitespace
         is allowed. Preserved by lossless canonical, stripped by
         strict canonical. See [[comments]]."""]]

  [child id=g-container-item title='container Item'
    [body
      """In the CXDM model (`spec/cxdm.md` §2), an Item is either an
         atom (one scalar) or a container (an element, array, or
         map). Sequences are flat — they are not containers. See
         [[container-atom]]."""]]

  [child id=g-content-addressable title='content-addressable'
    [body
      """Storage or lookup keyed by the hash of the content rather
         than an external name. CX is content-addressable by
         construction — the hash of the canonical bytes is the
         document's identity. See [[hash-use-cases]]."""]]

  [child id=g-cx-init title='cx_init'
    [body
      """The C ABI entry point bindings call once at module load to
         initialise the Boehm GC and runtime state. Idempotent. See
         [[c-abi]]."""]]

  [child id=g-cx-thread-register title='cx_thread_register'
    [body
      """The C ABI entry point a host-spawned thread calls before any
         other libcx call, to register itself with the GC. Paired
         with `cx_thread_unregister` at thread exit. Bindings
         auto-call from their Layer-1 wrappers. See
         [[ffi-thread-register]]."""]]

  [child id=g-cxcol title='CXCol'
    [body
      """CX's column-oriented streaming format. Pronounced "see-ex-col."
         Optimised for analytic scans; the same value model as native
         CX, projected column-wise. The canonical export target for
         the `:table` data shape. See [[cxcol]]."""]]

  [child id=g-cxdm title='CXDM'
    [body
      """CX Data Model — the abstract value model formalised in
         [`spec/cxdm.md`](../../spec/cxdm.md). Defines the eight
         scalar kinds, container kinds, sequence-flatness, equality,
         and the effective boolean value. The basis for every
         binding's value mapping."""]]

  [child id=g-cxpath title='CXPath'
    [body
      """The universal selector vocabulary. Same syntax for reading
         (`select_all`), iteration (`[?for]`), pattern matching
         (`[?match]`), and update focus (`[?modify]`). XPath 3.1
         aligned with deliberate divergences (see
         [`spec/cxpath_alignment.md`](../../spec/cxpath_alignment.md))
         and a value-kind. See [[cxpath]]."""]]

  [child id=g-data-bin title='data-bin'
    [body
      """The CX value wire format. Value-only (no comments, no
         original whitespace), schema-aware optional dictionary
         compression, page-compression wrapper. See [[data-bin]]."""]]

  [child id=g-data-language title='data language'
    [body
      """The non-directive subset of CX. Any element whose name does
         not start with `?`. Round-trips through every projection
         (JSON / YAML / TOML / XML / Markdown). See [[data]]."""]]

  [child id=g-date title='date'
    [body
      """The `:date` scalar kind. ISO 8601 calendar date with no time
         component: `2026-05-22`. See [[dates]]."""]]

  [child id=g-datetime title='datetime'
    [body
      """The `:datetime` scalar kind. ISO 8601 timestamp with
         timezone offset: `2026-05-22T14:30:00Z`. Resolution is
         nanoseconds; leap seconds are not represented. See
         [[datetime-detail]]."""]]

  [child id=g-default-ns title='default namespace'
    [body
      """A namespace declared with `xmlns='…'` (no prefix). Applies
         to unprefixed element names within its scope. See
         [[ns-default]]."""]]

  [child id=g-dict-encoding title='dictionary encoding'
    [body
      """A data-bin optional compression scheme that replaces
         repeated string values with a small integer index into a
         document-level table. Used by CXCol and Parquet bridge for
         categorical columns. See [[data-bin-schema-driven]]."""]]

  [child id=g-directive title='directive'
    [body
      """An element whose name starts with `?` (e.g. `[?for]`,
         `[?match]`, `[?modify]`). Interpreted by the evaluator
         rather than carried as data. Currently 40 normative
         directives. See [[directives]]."""]]

  [child id=g-doctype title='doctype'
    [body
      """A document-level declaration of the document's root element
         shape, optionally with public/system identifiers (XML
         legacy). CX carries doctype through the XML projection. See
         [[doctype]]."""]]

  [child id=g-document title='document'
    [body
      """The top-level CX value — either a single root element with
         any nested content, or a sequence of top-level elements
         (the multi-document form). Identity is the SHA-256 of its
         canonical bytes. See [[hash]]."""]]

  [child id=g-ebv title='effective boolean value (EBV)'
    [body
      """The truthiness coercion rule applied by `[?if]` and `[where …]`
         guards. Defined in [`spec/cxdm.md`](../../spec/cxdm.md)
         §4.6. Empty sequence / `false` / `0` / `''` / `null` are
         false; everything else is true. See [[if]]."""]]

  [child id=g-element title='element'
    [body
      """The basic CX data structure: a name, zero or more
         attributes, and a body. Written `[name attrs… body…]`.
         Every bracketed form is an element. See [[elements]]."""]]

  [child id=g-element-name title='element name'
    [body
      """The first token inside `[`. An identifier (or, rarely, a
         quoted string). Names beginning with `?` are directives.
         See [[names]]."""]]

  [child id=g-entity-reference title='entity reference'
    [body
      """An `&name;` token in prose / XML projection that expands to
         a registered character or string entity. CX recognises the
         XML five (`&lt;`, `&gt;`, `&amp;`, `&apos;`, `&quot;`) plus
         `&#NNNN;` numeric character references. See [[entity-refs]]."""]]

  [child id=g-equality title='equality (structural)'
    [body
      """Two CX values are equal iff their canonical bytes are
         identical. Equivalent to: tree-shape-equal after sorting
         attributes and applying the canonicalization rules. See
         [[canonical]]."""]]

  [child id=g-eval title='eval'
    [body
      """The C ABI entry point `cx_code_eval(doc, code, target_format)`.
         Evaluates a CX code expression against a document, returning
         a value in the requested format. See [[overview]] and
         [[c-abi]]."""]]

  [child id=g-expression-family title='expression family'
    [body
      """The five families of CX code expressions: select, iterate,
         dispatch, bind, update. Every directive lifts one family
         into a specific domain. See [[overview]]."""]]

  [child id=g-file-extension title='file extension'
    [body
      """`.cx` for general CX documents; `.cxs` for schemas; `.cxd`
         for data-only source (no directive bodies); `.cxcol` for
         CXCol columnar exports. The parser is the same for all
         four; the extension drives tooling defaults. See
         [[encoding]]."""]]

  [child id=g-float title='float'
    [body
      """The `:float` scalar kind. IEEE-754 double-precision by
         default; `:f32` and `:f64` are sized variants. See
         [[numbers]] and [[sized-types]]."""]]

  [child id=g-fn title='fn'
    [body
      """`[?fn]` — an anonymous function literal. A list of
         positional/labeled bindings followed by an expression
         body. See [[bindings]] in §6 and [[directives]]."""]]

  [child id=g-focus title='focus'
    [body
      """In `[?modify]`, the set of nodes selected by a CXPath
         expression at which an action is applied. Each focus node
         is updated independently; the result is a new document. See
         [[modify]]."""]]

  [child id=g-for title='for'
    [body
      """`[?for]` — iteration / comprehension. Binds a variable to
         each item in a CXPath, pattern, or sequence, and yields a
         value per iteration. See [[for]]."""]]

  [child id=g-hash title='hash (SHA-256)'
    [body
      """The 256-bit SHA-256 of a document's strict canonical bytes.
         Stable across machines, OS versions, and bindings.
         Short-form display uses the first 12 hex chars (96 bits) —
         see [[hash-truncation]] for the safety bound."""]]

  [child id=g-homoiconic title='homoiconic'
    [body
      """A language is homoiconic when its programs and its data use
         the same syntactic shape. CX is homoiconic by design — a
         directive `[?for]` parses and prints with the same rules as
         a data element `[user]`. See [[homoiconicity]]."""]]

  [child id=g-id-sigil title='id sigil (#)'
    [body
      """The `#name` attribute shortcut for `id='name'`. Declares a
         document-unique anchor for IDREF resolution. See [[id]]
         and [[id-anchors]]."""]]

  [child id=g-idref title='IDREF'
    [body
      """An attribute value that references another element's `id`
         attribute. Resolved on demand via `cx_idref_resolve`;
         cycles are detected and surfaced as `CXER0501`. See
         [[idref-resolution]]."""]]

  [child id=g-include title='include'
    [body
      """The `[?cx include path='…']` directive resolves and inlines
         another CX document. Capability-gated by default —
         `--profile untrusted` disables filesystem includes. See
         [[includes]]."""]]

  [child id=g-instance title='instance'
    [body
      """A concrete document that conforms to a schema. The schema
         describes the shape; the instance has the values. See
         [[schema-binding]]."""]]

  [child id=g-int title='int'
    [body
      """The `:int` scalar kind. 64-bit signed integer by default;
         `:i8`/`:i16`/`:i32`/`:i64` and unsigned variants are sized
         tags. See [[numbers]] and [[sized-types]]."""]]

  [child id=g-jsonl title='JSONL / NDJSON'
    [body
      """A streaming JSON format with one value per line. CX
         projects to JSONL when the root is a sequence; the
         projection guarantees one CX top-level item per output
         line. See [[jsonl]]."""]]

  [child id=g-lossless-canonical title='lossless canonical'
    [body
      """The form produced by `cx fmt`: pretty-printed, preserves
         comments and attribute order, but normalises quote choice
         and whitespace. Distinct from strict canonical, which
         strips comments and re-sorts attributes. See
         [[canon-lossless-strict]]."""]]

  [child id=g-lossy-projection title='lossy projection'
    [body
      """A projection that drops information the target format
         cannot represent. CX → JSON loses comments and CDATA; CX →
         CSV loses nested structure. Always reversible via the
         retained canonical CX form. See [[roundtrip]]."""]]

  [child id=g-manifest title='manifest'
    [body
      """The table of contents for the canonical guide, at
         `docs-src/canonical/manifest.cxd`. Lists every section
         file and its child anchors; renumbering is automatic from
         depth. See [[reading]]."""]]

  [child id=g-map title='map'
    [body
      """An unordered key-value container with unique string keys.
         Written `{k: v, k2: v2}`. Distinct from an element with
         attributes (an element is positional, named, and
         attributed; a map is just key-value). See [[map]]."""]]

  [child id=g-map-literal title='map literal'
    [body
      """The `{k: v, k2: v2}` form. Keys are strings or identifiers;
         values are any CX value. Map equality ignores entry order.
         See [[map]]."""]]

  [child id=g-match title='match'
    [body
      """`[?match]` — pattern dispatch. Single-arm form is an
         assertion that raises `CXER0100` on miss; multi-arm form
         selects the first matching `[case …]` clause.
         See [[match]]."""]]

  [child id=g-merge-sigil title='merge sigil (*)'
    [body
      """The `*name` form on an attribute or element body splices
         the content of the named anchor. The complement of the
         anchor sigil `&name`. See [[merge]]."""]]

  [child id=g-modify title='modify'
    [body
      """`[?modify]` — pure-functional update. Takes a document, a
         CXPath focus, and an action clause (`[set …]` / `[delete]`
         / …); returns a new document. See [[modify]]."""]]

  [child id=g-multi-arm-match title='multi-arm match'
    [body
      """The N-arm form of `[?match]` with `[case …]` / `[when …]` /
         `[else …]` arms and optional `[where …]` guards.
         See [[match]]."""]]

  [child id=g-namespace title='namespace'
    [body
      """An XML-aligned grouping mechanism that scopes element and
         attribute names with a URI. Declared by `xmlns:prefix='uri'`
         (or `xmlns='uri'` for a default). See [[namespaces]]."""]]

  [child id=g-ns-prefix title='namespace prefix'
    [body
      """The short string used to refer to a namespace in element /
         attribute names (e.g. `svg:rect`, where `svg` is the prefix
         and `rect` is the local name). See [[ns-prefix-decl]]."""]]

  [child id=g-node title='node'
    [body
      """An addressable position in a CX tree. Every element,
         attribute, scalar, comment, and processing instruction is
         a node. CXPath returns sequences of nodes. See
         [[cxpath]]."""]]

  [child id=g-null title='null'
    [body
      """The reserved literal denoting the absence of a value.
         Distinct from missing (an attribute that is not present at
         all). Its EBV is false. See [[null]]."""]]

  [child id=g-nfc title='NFC normalization'
    [body
      """Unicode Normalization Form C (canonical composition). All
         CX identifiers and string scalars are NFC-normalized at
         parse time. See [[identifiers]]."""]]

  [child id=g-parallel title='parallel'
    [body
      """The CX concurrency posture — `[?map par=true]` and
         `[?reduce par=true]` (and `[?for ... par=true]`) distribute
         work across bounded worker pools; immutability makes the
         result deterministic. See [[parallelism]]."""]]

  [child id=g-parquet title='parquet'
    [body
      """Apache Parquet — the columnar storage format CX exports
         to and imports from via the Parquet bridge. CXCol is the
         in-memory analogue; Parquet is the on-disk
         interchange. See [[parquet-bridge]]."""]]

  [child id=g-parquet-bridge title='parquet bridge'
    [body
      """The libcx subsystem that reads and writes Apache Parquet
         files via Arrow. Capability bit 12. See
         [[parquet-bridge]]."""]]

  [child id=g-pattern title='pattern'
    [body
      """A CX value with embedded binding variables (e.g.
         `[user id=$i]`) that matches a target value structurally
         and binds the variables on success. Used by `[?match]`,
         `[?for]`, and `[?modify]`. See [[patterns]]."""]]

  [child id=g-pattern-generator title='pattern generator'
    [body
      """A pattern used at the source of a `[?for]` to enumerate
         matching positions in a document. Equivalent to a CXPath
         that yields the same node set. See [[patterns]]."""]]

  [child id=g-pipe title='pipe (|)'
    [body
      """The `|` operator threads the value on its left into the
         expression on its right, bound to `$1`. Canonical form
         desugars to `[?pipe …]`. See [[pipe]]."""]]

  [child id=g-pi title='processing instruction (PI)'
    [body
      """An XML-only directive carried as a node (e.g.
         `<?xml-stylesheet …?>`). CX preserves PIs through the XML
         projection. See [[xml-pi]]."""]]

  [child id=g-projection title='projection'
    [body
      """A surface other than canonical CX (JSON, YAML, TOML, XML,
         Markdown, CSV, JSONL). Every projection round-trips —
         CX → projection → CX produces byte-identical canonical
         bytes. See [[surfaces]]."""]]

  [child id=g-prose title='prose'
    [body
      """Mixed-content body — text interleaved with elements. The
         shape that powers Markdown and prose-heavy XML. See
         [[prose]]."""]]

  [child id=g-pure-update title='pure-functional update'
    [body
      """An update that returns a new value without mutating the
         input. CX's `[?modify]` is pure-functional; unchanged
         branches are shared with the input via the standard
         persistent-tree technique. See [[pure-updates]]."""]]

  [child id=g-quotes title='quotes (single / double / triple)'
    [body
      """Three string forms: single-quoted `'…'` (escapes
         supported), double-quoted `"…"` (same), and triple-quoted
         `'''…'''` or `"""…"""` (multiline, whitespace-preserving,
         no escape needed for the other quote characters). See
         [[strings]]."""]]

  [child id=g-regex title='regex'
    [body
      """The regular-expression dialect used by CX builtins. CX
         ships an RE2-equivalent engine; the dialect is documented
         in [`spec/regex.md`](../../spec/regex.md). See
         [[string-builtins]]."""]]

  [child id=g-reserved-token title='reserved token'
    [body
      """An identifier the parser refuses to accept as an element
         or attribute name: `true`, `false`, `null`, and the
         directive head tokens. See [[reserved-tokens]]."""]]

  [child id=g-resilience-directive title='resilience directive'
    [body
      """One of the six failure-handling wrappers (`[?retry]`,
         `[?timeout]`, `[?circuit-breaker]`, `[?fallback]`,
         `[?rate-limit]`, `[?bulkhead]`). See [[resilience]]."""]]

  [child id=g-schema title='schema'
    [body
      """A CX document (`.cxs`) describing the allowed shape of
         another CX document. The schema language is documented
         in [`spec/schema.md`](../../spec/schema.md). See
         [[schema]]."""]]

  [child id=g-scope title='scope'
    [body
      """The lexical region in which a binding is visible.
         `[?let]` introduces a scope; namespace prefix
         declarations have a scope; anchors are document-scoped.
         See [[let]] and [[namespaces]]."""]]

  [child id=g-sequence title='sequence'
    [body
      """A flat, ordered collection of values. Written `(a, b, c)`.
         Distinct from an array — a sequence is not a container;
         nesting a sequence inside a sequence flattens. See
         [[seq]] and [[seq-flat]]."""]]

  [child id=g-sequence-flat title='sequence-flat principle'
    [body
      """CX sequences never nest. `(1, (2, 3), 4)` is identical to
         `(1, 2, 3, 4)`. Arrays and maps preserve nesting; sequences
         do not. See [[seq-flat]]."""]]

  [child id=g-sequence-literal title='sequence literal'
    [body
      """The `(a, b, c)` form. Identical to an evaluator-returned
         sequence. See [[seq]]."""]]

  [child id=g-sigil title='sigil'
    [body
      """A leading punctuation character that prefixes an
         identifier and changes its interpretation: `&` (anchor),
         `*` (merge), `#` (id), `:` (type tag),
         `$` (binding variable), `?` (directive). See [[sigils]]."""]]

  [child id=g-signed-canonical title='signed canonical'
    [body
      """A canonical CX document accompanied by an external
         signature over its strict canonical bytes. Not part of
         the core spec; built atop the hash. See [[hash-use-cases]]."""]]

  [child id=g-sized-type-tag title='sized type tag'
    [body
      """An explicit numeric type prefix: `:i8`, `:i16`, `:i32`,
         `:i64`, `:u8`, `:u16`, `:u32`, `:u64`, `:f32`, `:f64`.
         Required when the host binding needs a specific width.
         See [[sized-types]]."""]]

  [child id=g-slot title='slot (positional, labeled)'
    [body
      """A position inside a directive's argument list. Positional
         slots come first; labeled slots use the `:label value`
         form (per `spec/grammar.ebnf [127e]`). Slot syntax is
         exclusive to directives — on data elements use
         `name=value` attributes. See [[directives]]."""]]

  [child id=g-strict-canonical title='strict canonical'
    [body
      """The form produced by `cx canonical` — strips comments,
         re-sorts attributes lexicographically, normalises quote
         choice, normalises whitespace, NFC-normalises identifiers
         and strings. Hash input. See [[canon-lossless-strict]]."""]]

  [child id=g-streaming title='streaming'
    [body
      """Processing a document without loading it entirely into
         memory. CX's streaming evaluator handles documents up to
         the host's filesystem size; gate 15 measures
         the throughput floor. See
         [[streaming]]."""]]

  [child id=g-structural-sharing title='structural sharing'
    [body
      """The persistent-tree technique that lets `[?modify]`
         return a new document in O(log n) by reusing the
         unchanged branches of the input. See [[pure-updates]]."""]]

  [child id=g-table-shape title='table data shape (:table)'
    [body
      """A type tag that marks an element as a typed columnar
         table — homogeneous rows with a declared header. The
         in-memory bridge to CXCol and Parquet. See [[table-shape]]."""]]

  [child id=g-template title='template'
    [body
      """A CX value with embedded code expressions that produces
         a derived value when evaluated. In CX there is no
         "template language" — code and data share one shape, so
         every CX value is potentially a template. See [[code]]."""]]

  [child id=g-threading-register title='threading register'
    [body
      """The combined operation of `cx_thread_register` (on
         thread start) and `cx_thread_unregister` (on thread
         exit), required for host-spawned threads that call libcx
         directly. Bindings auto-wrap. See [[ffi-thread-register]]."""]]

  [child id=g-time title='time'
    [body
      """The wall-clock-time-of-day scalar kind. Not a separate
         scalar in CXDM — represented as a datetime with the
         epoch-1970 date placeholder when carried at the wire
         level. See [[datetime-detail]]."""]]

  [child id=g-timezone title='time zone'
    [body
      """The offset-from-UTC component of a datetime scalar.
         Required on the wire; absence is parsed as UTC. See
         [[datetime-detail]]."""]]

  [child id=g-type-tag title='type tag'
    [body
      """An explicit `:name` prefix on a scalar that forces a
         specific kind: `:int`, `:str`, `:date`, `:bytes`, `:u32`,
         etc. See [[bodies]] and [[sized-types]]."""]]

  [child id=g-utf8 title='UTF-8'
    [body
      """The required source encoding for every CX file. The
         parser rejects non-UTF-8 input; the BOM is consumed
         silently if present. See [[encoding]]."""]]

  [child id=g-value title='value'
    [body
      """Any CX shape — a scalar, an element, a sequence, an
         array, or a map. The eval pipeline produces values; the
         data model is a value model. See [[overview]]."""]]

  [child id=g-value-comparison title='value comparison'
    [body
      """The CXPath comparison operators (`=`, `<`, `<=`, etc.)
         applied to scalar values. Numerically aware
         (`@n=42` matches both int and float 42); string
         comparison is codepoint-wise. See [[cxpath]]."""]]

  [child id=g-wasm title='wasm'
    [body
      """The WebAssembly build of libcx used by the playground
         and any browser-hosted CX tooling. Exposes a subset of
         the C ABI plus `_cx_code_diagram` and friends. Two
         artifacts: `libcx-async.js` (Asyncify, no
         pthreads — works under file:// and any HTTP host),
         `libcx-pthreads.{js,wasm}` (real OS threads via
         SharedArrayBuffer — requires HTTP with COOP/COEP
         headers). The playground auto-selects based on
         `crossOriginIsolated`. See [[g-playground]] and
         [[wasm-story]]."""]]

  [child id=g-playground title='playground'
    [body
      """A constrained demonstration surface for CX inside the
         browser, not the performance target. Three delivery
         modes: GitHub Pages static (HTTPS), local clone file://
         (double-click `playground.html`), and `make guide-http`
         (V veb server with cross-origin isolation enabled). Only
         the third mode runs `par=true` examples on real OS threads;
         the first two run sequentially under the same surface.
         Production CX (CLI, language bindings, libcx as shared
         library) has no browser-environment overhead. See
         [[wasm-story]] for the full framing."""]]

  [child id=g-whitespace-preservation title='whitespace preservation'
    [body
      """The `xml:space='preserve'` attribute scopes the
         preservation of internal runs of whitespace inside an
         element body. The default is collapse. See
         [[xml-space]]."""]]

  [child id=g-xml-space title='xml:space'
    [body
      """The reserved attribute that controls whitespace
         collapsing in an element body. Values `default` and
         `preserve`. See [[xml-space]]."""]]

  [child id=g-xmlns title='xmlns'
    [body
      """The reserved attribute family that declares namespace
         prefix bindings: `xmlns:svg='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'`
         binds `svg` for the element's scope. See
         [[namespaces]]."""]]]
